  "name": "Hellfire Reprimand makes Hellfire Imps launch Firebolt on hit (#9057)",
  "contract": "Hellfire Reprimand (706565, ProcChance 20): \"Your Hellfire Imps now have a 20% chance on hit to launch a firebolt\" (800444) that also reduces the enemy's attack power (578318). The talent is a passive whose only effects are SPELL_EFFECT_ASCENSION_APPLY_AURA_TO_SUMMONS, so the knight learns it without holding it as an applied aura of their own. A Hellfire Imp lasts 12 s and Call: Hellfire Imp has a 10 s cooldown, so fifteen imps called back to back, each sent at the enemy while the knight stays idle, swing at it for about 160 s. At one swing per 2 s that is about 75 swings; the 6-imp run that first passed launched 4 Firebolts, which at 20% is about 20 damaging swings, so 15 imps give at least about 45 even at that low rate and the chance that none launches a Firebolt is 0.8^45, below 0.01%.",
